        "answer": {
          "short": "$4x^2+20x+101-\\dfrac{45}{x-5}$",
          "worked": "Insert the missing term $0x^2$. Divide the leading terms, multiply by $x-5$ and subtract at each stage.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(4x^3+0x^2+x-550)-(4x^3-20x^2)&=20x^2+x-550\\\\\n(20x^2+x-550)-(20x^2-100x)&=101x-550\\\\\n(101x-550)-(101x-505)&=-45.\n\\end{aligned}$$\nThe quotient terms are $4x^2$, $20x$ and $101$, so the blanks are $4x^2$ and $101$.\n$$\\frac{4x^3+x-550}{x-5}=4x^2+20x+101-\\frac{45}{x-5}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
