            "id": "p37-q3-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "$(x^3-5x+3)\\div(x-2)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$x^2+2x-1+\\dfrac{1}{x-2}$",
              "worked": "Insert $0x^2$. Successive leading-term divisions give $x^2$, $2x$ and $-1$. Multiply each by $x-2$ and subtract:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(x^3+0x^2-5x+3)-(x^3-2x^2)&=2x^2-5x+3\\\\\n(2x^2-5x+3)-(2x^2-4x)&=-x+3\\\\\n(-x+3)-(-x+2)&=1.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\frac{x^3-5x+3}{x-2}=x^2+2x-1+\\frac{1}{x-2}.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 70
          },
          {
            "id": "p37-q3-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$(2x^3+x^2-11)\\div(x+1)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$2x^2-x+1-\\dfrac{12}{x+1}$",
              "worked": "Insert $0x$. Successive leading-term divisions give $2x^2$, $-x$ and $1$. Multiply each by $x+1$ and subtract:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(2x^3+x^2+0x-11)-(2x^3+2x^2)&=-x^2-11\\\\\n(-x^2+0x-11)-(-x^2-x)&=x-11\\\\\n(x-11)-(x+1)&=-12.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\frac{2x^3+x^2-11}{x+1}=2x^2-x+1-\\frac{12}{x+1}.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 70
          },
          {
            "id": "p37-q3-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x^3-3}{2x-4}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$x^2+2x+4+\\dfrac{13}{2x-4}$",
              "worked": "Insert $0x^2$ and $0x$. Successive leading-term divisions by $2x$ give $x^2$, $2x$ and $4$. Multiply each by $2x-4$ and subtract:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(2x^3+0x^2+0x-3)-(2x^3-4x^2)&=4x^2-3\\\\\n(4x^2+0x-3)-(4x^2-8x)&=8x-3\\\\\n(8x-3)-(8x-16)&=13.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\frac{2x^3-3}{2x-4}=x^2+2x+4+\\frac{13}{2x-4}.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 70
          },
          {
            "id": "p37-q3-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3x^4-4x^3+4x-9}{x-2}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$3x^3+2x^2+4x+12+\\dfrac{15}{x-2}$",
              "worked": "Insert $0x^2$. Successive leading-term divisions give $3x^3$, $2x^2$, $4x$ and $12$. Multiply each by $x-2$ and subtract:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(3x^4-4x^3+0x^2+4x-9)-(3x^4-6x^3)&=2x^3+4x-9\\\\\n(2x^3+0x^2+4x-9)-(2x^3-4x^2)&=4x^2+4x-9\\\\\n(4x^2+4x-9)-(4x^2-8x)&=12x-9\\\\\n(12x-9)-(12x-24)&=15.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\frac{3x^4-4x^3+4x-9}{x-2}=3x^3+2x^2+4x+12+\\frac{15}{x-2}.$$",
